q("fi-006", B, 1, PAT, "Which of the following ways will reduce the friction when moving a heavy box?", "Putting the box on wheels", [W("Making the floor rougher", "increases", "A rougher floor means more friction."), W("Putting sand on the floor", "increases", "Sand makes the floor rougher, so there is more friction."), W("Gluing rubber under the box", "increases", "Rubber grips the floor, so there is more friction.")], ["Wheels roll instead of rubbing, so there is much less friction."], None)
q("fi-007", B, 1, PAT, "Which of these activities needs friction?", "Walking on a path without slipping", [W("Sliding down a slide quickly", "wrong-need", "A slide works best with little friction."), W("Skating on smooth ice", "wrong-need", "Skating needs little friction."), W("Pushing a toy car on a smooth table", "wrong-need", "A car moves further when there is little friction.")], ["Friction between the shoe and the ground stops us from slipping when we walk."], None)
